SUMMARY:Mysteries of matter: new experiments to unpick the nature of dark m
 atter (Dr Daniel Johnson)
LOCATION:Poynting Large Lecture Theatre\, Physics Building (R13)
DESCRIPTION:Dr Daniel Johnson\nInstitute of Physics Public Lecture Series\n
 \nContrary to its name\, there is nothing hidden about dark matter. It's t
 here in plain sight\, dramatically changing the way galaxies move and impr
 inted all over the incredible pictures astronomers take of the cosmos. But
 \, whilst we know for sure that it is there\, we have no idea what it's ma
 de of and that makes particle physicists deeply uncomfortable. This evenin
 g we will explore new methods to tease out truths about the particle ident
 ity of dark matter\, and how new experiments might soon shed light on this
  mysterious matter that\, overwhelmingly\, dominates the 'stuff' in the Un
 iverse.\n\nDetails: https://www.birmingham.ac.uk/about/college-of-engineer
 ing-and-physical-sciences/physics-and-astronomy/outreach-and-schools-liais
 on/outreach-for-secondary-schools/iop-public-lecture-series
CATEGORIES:Institute of Physics Public Lecture Series
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://www.birmingham.ac.uk/about/college-of-engineering-and-physical-
 sciences/physics-and-astronomy/outreach-and-schools-liaison/outreach-for-s
 econdary-schools/iop-public-lecture-series
END:VEVENT
