SUMMARY:Is it a star? Is it a planet? No\, it's a brown dwarf! (Dr Jenni Fr
 ench)
LOCATION:Poynting Large Lecture Theatre\, Physics Building (R13)
DESCRIPTION:Dr Jenni French\nInstitute of Physics Public Lecture Series\n\n
 Brown dwarfs are the Universe’s awkward middle child\, not quite a star\
 , not quite a planet\, but they are fascinating in their own right. Acting
  as the intermediary objects between planets and stars\, brown dwarfs have
  complex atmospheres and act as natural laboratories for a plethora of exo
 planet science. This talk explores brown dwarfs\, what they are\, how we f
 ind them\, and why they’re so interesting\, as well as how you can get i
 nvolved in their discovery.\n\nDetails: https://www.birmingham.ac.uk/about
 /college-of-engineering-and-physical-sciences/physics-and-astronomy/outrea
 ch-and-schools-liaison/outreach-for-secondary-schools/iop-public-lecture-s
 eries
CATEGORIES:Institute of Physics Public Lecture Series
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://www.birmingham.ac.uk/about/college-of-engineering-and-physical-
 sciences/physics-and-astronomy/outreach-and-schools-liaison/outreach-for-s
